    "referenceImplementation": "OpenSSL",
    "referenceImplementationNote": "OpenSSL is the fixed reference implementation for every entry. This measures adoption in one open-source library, not the earliest implementation anywhere, overall deployment, or FIPS module certification. Another library may have implemented a feature earlier. Protocols and algorithm families are explicitly named; support is not a claim that every optional feature or mode in a specification is implemented.",
    "curationNote": "Curated, non-exhaustive completed transitions. Every row cites final specification publication and release-pinned OpenSSL change notes. RFC header dates are month-precision and encoded as the first of the month, explicitly marked standardDatePrecision=month; these are not observed first-day publication dates. Month-start encoding can overstate a lag by up to 30 days and is material for short lags. NIST document-history dates and OpenSSL stable-release dates retain verified day precision. Preprints, Internet-Drafts, FIPS drafts, prereleases, third-party providers, and planned releases are not endpoints. Changes in the selected sample can change the medians without implying a field-wide causal trend.",
    "generated": "2026-10-28",
    "coverageNote": "Bounded primary-source audit of all legacy rows and selected omitted transitions, including stable releases through OpenSSL 4.1.0. Not a census of all OpenSSL cryptographic features.",
    "readingCaveat": "This selected sample contains completed transitions, not a field-wide census. RFC dates use the first day of their publication month; lags can be overstated by up to 30 days. Historical additions change the sample, not observed field acceleration."
  },
